ATION maintenance mode\n\nReturn only a complete replacement Markdown evidence-integration ledger whose\nfirst line is exactly `# Evidence Integration Ledger`. Do not take an ordinary task\naction. Integrate source-grounded findings, qualifications, cross-source\nrelationships, requirement bindings R01-R12, contradictions, and unresolved\nevidence useful for the authoritative task.\n\nThe output is model-authored and lossy. It cannot authorize readiness or\nsubmission. Replace prior material rather than appending indefinitely. Keep it\nunder the hard 1600-token limit. The only evidence source\nIDs you may cite are: S02, S03, S04, S08, S13. Source identities elsewhere in the task are\nnot evidence unless they are in that allowlist.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task\n\n# Task: bounded-agent architecture decision package\n\nProduce two exact deliverables from the source catalog:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe decision is for the next phase of a bounded-context agent research program.\nIt must distinguish mechanisms that earned a role from mechanisms that were\nonly behaviorally active, locally harmful, blocked, or still untested.\n\n## Evidence ledger requirements\n\nThe ledger must begin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and contain rows or\nsections for `R01` through `R12`. Each requirement entry must state a current\ndisposition, cite exact observed sources as `[SNN]`, preserve important\nqualifications or conflicts, and identify unresolved evidence where present.\n\n## Decision document requirements\n\nUse exactly these level-two headings, in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision and scope`\n2. `## Earned mechanical substrate`\n3. `## Information interactions and failure migration`\n4. `## State, relationships, chronology, and control`\n5. `## Runtime policy`\n6. `## Experimental roadmap`\n7. `## Verification, readiness, and governance`\n8. `## Uncertainties and falsifiers`\n\nThe document must be 1,600–2,200 words excluding exact `[SNN]` citations and\nmust use at least ten distinct source IDs. It must cite `S02`, `S03`, `S04`,\n`S08`, and `S13`.\n\nThe package must substantively cover these twelve requirements:\n\n- `R01`: exact external custody and reopenability;\n- `R02`: response/control reserves and positive-savings relief;\n- `R03`: capacity, delivery, action, effect uptake, quality, and closure as\n  distinct boundaries;\n- `R04`: recoverability, residency, behavioral accessibility, and working-set\n  adequacy as distinct properties;\n- `R05`: chronology's external and resident lifecycle;\n- `R06`: cache/prefill and decision-bandwidth costs;\n- `R07`: semantic derivatives as endogenous demand/control inputs;\n- `R08`: the source-digest negative and progress-state false-closure risk;\n- `R09`: host/model ownership supported by manager and paging results;\n- `R10`: E40's detached-sidecar versus task-artifact gap;\n- `R11`: an interaction-first roadmap with fresh transfer and stopping rules;\n- `R12`: evaluation/readiness lineage and candidate-bound currentness.\n\nDo not claim that artifact coupling, notes, digests, progress state, model-owned\neviction, automatic phase discovery, or a general architecture is already\nvalidated. Name conditions that would falsify the recommended next policy.\n\n\n# Prior accepted integration ledger\n\n# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Exact External Custody and Reopenability**\nDisposition: Qualified mechanical substrate earned. Exact external custody maintains byte integrity, but reopenability is reactive rather than scheduled. Scheduled low-occupancy reentry failed to earn a default role [S02]. Reactive exact reentry remains an unpromoted fallback for insufficient declared relief [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No fresh-task scout has validated proactive reopen strategies under high pressure [S02].\n\n**R02: Response/Control Reserves and Positive-Savings Relief**\nDisposition: Deterministic first-fit pressure relief is qualified. It is strictly restricted to prospectively rendered, strictly positive-savings substitutions under a frozen scan order [S02]. Reactive reentry activates only when declared relief is insufficient [S02]. Unresolved evidence: The I1 relief event replaced a one-line body with a receipt costing 79 more tokens, remaining descriptive rather than validating broader utility [S02].\n\n**R03: Capacity, Delivery, Action, Effect Uptake, Quality, and Closure**\nDisposition: Distinct boundaries identified but not jointly validated. The I1–I4 run activated batch ingress and work sidecars, yet no mutation, effect uptake, check, or submission occurred [S02]. Capacity remained active but non-terminal; call budget became terminal while evidence remained incomplete [S02]. Unresolved evidence: Joint effects of these boundaries within a complete bounded trajectory remain untested [S02].\n\n**R04: Recoverability, Residency, Behavioral Accessibility, and Working-Set Adequacy**\nDisposition: Distinct properties acknowledged. Value is conditional on task phase, co-resident set, and regime, not intrinsic [S03]. Semantic compression lowers resident cost but introduces task-dependent loss [S03]. Unresolved evidence: No scalar weights are earned for these properties; costs must be reported as vectors, not aggregates [S03].\n\n**R05: Chronology’s External and Resident Lifecycle**\nDisposition: Ordinary chronology is qualified while healthy. History growth causes useful exact evidence to lose co-residency, increasing reopening churn [S03]. Unresolved evidence: Interaction between chronology lifecycle and semantic persistence remains untested in fresh trajectories [S02].\n\n**R06: Cache/Prefill and Decision-Bandwidth Costs**\nDisposition: Costs are path-dependent and partly endogenous. Cache invalidation and prefill latency are distinct accounting factors [S03]. The I1–I4 run consumed 2,112,973 serialized tokens, qualifying action transport but not downstream utility [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No mathematical chaos demonstrated; only seed sensitivity and changing bottlenecks observed [S03].\n\n**R07: Semantic Derivatives as Endogenous Demand/Control Inputs**\nDisposition: Semantic derivatives are endogenous demand inputs. A newly produced digest may be valuable only after raw source leaves residency [S03]. Unresolved evidence: The failed source-bound semantic residue route (exceeding 256-token budget at 310 tokens) is closed; no v3 allowed [S02].\n\n**R08: Source-Digest Negative and Progress-State False-Closure Risk**\nDisposition: High risk confirmed. The first proposed interaction failed its prospective apparatus gate before actor trajectory ran [S02]. Provenance repairs improved acceptance, but budget constraints closed the dedicated residue route [S02]. Unresolved evidence: False-closure risk in progress-state remains unquantified across independent worlds [S02].\n\n**R09: Host/Model Ownership Supported by Manager and Paging Results**\nDisposition: Host-owned response and control reserves are earned. Manager and paging results support host ownership, but model-owned eviction is not validated [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No general architecture validation; only local mechanism evidence exists [S02].\n\n**R10: E40’s Detached-Sidecar versus Task-Artifact Gap**\nDisposition: Gap confirmed. The work sidecar produced genuine cross-source prose but shed earlier citations, citing only four sources despite 13/14 allowlists [S02]. It functioned as semantic state, not an exact partial charter or independently checkable task artifact [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No successful transfer of sidecar content to durable work-product externalization [S02].\n\n**R11: Interaction-First Roadmap with Fresh Transfer and Stopping Rules**\nDisposition: Active route defined. The next candidate interaction is evidence-ingress bandwidth × cumulative task-native work externalization [S02]. Stopping rules are frozen; no v3 for failed designs [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No whole configuration has yet shown meaningful joint effect transferring to an independent world [S02].\n\n**R12: Evaluation/Readiness Lineage and Candidate-Bound Currentness**\nDisposition: Independent candidate/task/evidence-bound evaluation is mandatory common governance [S02]. The I1–I4 run is frozen for measurement at a specific commit hash [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No readiness lineage established for general architecture; only local negatives qualify [S02].\n\n# Exact newly externalized observation\n\n{\"object_id\":\"source:S13:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"6f9a5d30b56496cce7010b8055392f4a1f33930959d672217e83b22c189028fd\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S13\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S13_H05_CORRECTION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6f9a5d30b56496cce7010b8055392f4a1f33930959d672217e83b22c189028fd\",\"source_size_bytes\":2276,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# H05 artifact-disposition reconciliation\n\nDate: 2026-08-22\n\n## Finding\n\nThe H05 raw behavioral contrast is valid, but its original artifact disposition\nwas wrong.\n\nThe treated actor submitted candidate ID\n`38893b4df5afc252a356ff5ab79a1dcda6330b7934a252a67d2759499eb4aac6`,\nfile SHA-256\n`888c142abcad4c3bd9081960bdb18b7402be6415c03b456033ed3c7aed134d39`.\nThose exact bytes had already been audited at construction-reentry donor commit\n`68a4b0b04c4557dcc459b42822e804f241565757` as a **strong partial** artifact.\n\nThe prior frozen table contained 12 substantive requirement groups:\n\n- 10 met;\n- apparatus-correction coverage partial; and\n- factual precision about the timing of 11 seed-42 reopens partial.\n\nThe candidate also satisfied the separate file-scope constraint. It was not a\ncomplete task artifact.\n\n## Corrected H05 interpretation\n\nThe literal sequence remains:\n\n```text\nbyte-identical control\n-> resident candidate reread\n\n169-token progress state in 464-token package\n-> admitted submit\n-> unchanged strong-partial candidate\n```\n\nThe package was behaviorally active. Its trajectory utility was negative at\nthis defect-bearing boundary because it induced closure without identifying or\nrepairing either known partial requirement.\n\nThis is the first direct not-ready discrimination result for H05. It is\nconsistent with a recent self-authored closure cue and does not establish safe\nprogress reconciliation.\n\n## Error classification\n\nThe H05 post-run review checked headline facts at a coarser granularity and did\nnot reconcile the candidate hash against the existing frozen adjudication. The\nerror is investigator-side artifact classification. It does not invalidate:\n\n- the three model calls;\n- literal actions and results;\n- candidate custody;\n- tokenizer receipts;\n- replay;\n- tests; or\n- run seals.\n\nThe standalone correction is published at commit\n`a3422cca49cb882ec252ba84903b856ba3cafc24`.\n\n## Governance rule\n\nFuture control/progress utility experiments must freeze an independent\ncandidate-readiness adjudication before maintenance output or treated actor\nbehavior is observed. Candidate hashes must be reconciled against every prior\nadjudication in the donor lineage. Submission is positive only when that frozen\nadjudication says closure is appropriate.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":3854,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":2764,"prompt_ms":3511.625,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.2704866136034731,"prompt_per_second":787.0999893211832,"predicted_n":1091,"predicted_ms":36359.939,"predicted_per_token_ms":33.35774220183486,"predicted_per_second":29.978048092984977}},"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":2764,"prompt_ms":3511.625,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.2704866136034731,"prompt_per_second":787.0999893211832,"predicted_n":1091,"predicted_ms":36359.939,"predicted_per_token_